the demonstration in Paris began outside  the French Senate protestors want  senators to change a proposed law that  would allow access to either F for  single and gay women not just those in a  heterosexual couple  they say the French government's new  bioethics bill would deprive children of  the father and destroy the moral fabric  of French society and some worry could  be expanded to legalize surrogacy the  law doesn't take into account at all the  right of the child or its future it only  accounts for a woman's desire to have a  child it's important to defend the  family unit a mother and a father for  the balance of French society and for  children's welfare the March was  peaceful but police officers broke up a  small counter protest the controversial  bill has divided opinion in September  French MPs approved it but only after a  fiery debate or the report how dare you  decide to inscribe in to know that a  child be deprived of a father this  shocks me yes I mean notional you are  playing with fire go to protest against  gay marriage but for supporters of the  proposed law they say it would be a  victory for women's rights when she  reached her mid-30s benedict blase  wanted to become a mother as a single  woman she was unable to access ICF in  France so she travelled to Denmark and  Portugal where the treatment is legally  available to all women I felt out low in  my own country because I just wanted a  baby and that right was okay in other  European countries but not in France  Benedict's son is now 14 months old  father first say all that matters is  love and though the fact that he was  wanted  if the bioethics bill becomes law it  will fulfill one of French presidents  Emmanuel macron campaign promises and  create hope for single and gay women who  dream of becoming a parent but these  protesters say  they won't give up their battle to  protect traditional family values and  stop the legislation from being passed  Natasha Butler al-jazeera Paris
 

